From c0d6004ecbdc045412200c7bbc06dff18ef95323 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sijie52 <sijie5452@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:58:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(c): model C value, pointer, control-flow, linkage and
 libc semantics

- Declared types (c-types.ts): identifiers are annotated with their
  lexically scoped declared type; struct field types and typedefs are
  indexed.
- Struct by value: declaration/assignment copies, by-value parameters and
  *ps = b copy the aggregate; fields are independent storage, nested
  structs and array members are copied recursively, pointer members keep
  sharing their pointee.
- Pointers: &x of a scalar/pointer variable is a distinct address value
  bound to x's location; *e reads and writes the location e currently
  points to, so multi-level dereference, rebinding and char *** out
  parameters resolve level by level.
- Control flow: per-call control state; statements after
  return/break/continue/goto are unreachable until the matching goto
  target, goto states are joined at the label, if/switch/loops propagate
  abrupt completion, C integer constant expressions are folded,
  &&/||/?: short-circuit, and a one-branch if ending in return does not
  leak its writes past the if.
- Linkage: header static functions are visible per translation unit
  (CompileUnit._meta.includes); same-name definitions in undecided #if
  branches are kept as a union instead of first-wins.
- libc: full overwrite replaces dst taint, partial writes keep it, length
  0 writes nothing, format functions only read the arguments the format
  consumes, sscanf writes per conversion. atoi/strtol/strlen results and
  %d-formatted text carry numeric taint: ignored by injection sinks,
  still reported by length and format-string sinks.
- Compile configuration for parser-C: --cDefine, --cUndefine, --cTarget
  (default linux), --cUnknownMacros cover|undefined, --cIncludeDir.
- Regression: test/c/test-c-semantics.ts runs 78 paired cases.
